{"type": "tool_use", "name": "write_file", "input": {"path": "outputs/t6_matrix.md", "content": "# Workstation Comparison Table\n\n| Attribute | Aurora 14 | Summit X15 | Vantage Pro 16 |\n|-----------|-----------|------------|----------------|\n| CPU | Helix H9 AI, 16 cores | Helix H7 AI, 12 cores | Corvex X12, 14 cores |\n| GPU | Vireo V8000 Pro, 16 GB | Vireo V6000, 8 GB | Vireo V9000, 24 GB |\n| Max Memory | 128 GB (user-upgradeable) | 96 GB | 64 GB (soldered) |\n| Max Storage | 4 TB NVMe | not stated | 2 TB |\n| Display | 14-inch OLED, 2880 x 1800, 120 Hz | 15.6-inch OLED, 3840 x 2400, 60 Hz | 16-inch IPS, 2560 x 1600, 165 Hz |\n| Weight | 1.65 kg | 1.95 kg | 2.30 kg |\n| Battery | 86 Wh | not stated | 99 Wh |\n| Ports | 2 x Thunderbolt 5, 1 x USB-A, HDMI 2.1, SD card reader | 2 x Thunderbolt 4, 1 x USB-A, HDMI 2.1 | not stated |\n\n## Aurora 14 Differentiators\n\n1. **Smallest form factor** - At 1.65 kg and 14-inch, the Aurora 14 is the lightest and most portable option, 0.30 kg lighter than the Summit X15 and 0.65 kg lighter than the Vantage Pro 16.\n\n2. **Thunderbolt 5 connectivity** - The Aurora 14 includes Thunderbolt 5 ports, the fastest interface in the lineup. The Summit X15 only offers Thunderbolt 4, and the Vantage Pro 16 does not list ports at all.\n\n3. **Highest memory expandability** - With 128 GB max memory and user-upgradeable slots, the Aurora 14 offers the highest memory ceiling and upgrade path compared to the Summit X15 (96 GB) and Vantage Pro 16 (64 GB soldered, no upgrade path).\n"}, "timestamp": 1790808864303}
